# OpenAI Codex tooling (cross-tool agent config, kept local)
AGENTS.md
.codex/

# Content-writing notes that were sitting under public/images/**/content/.
# They are prose, not assets, and anything under public/ is publicly served —
# so they are kept in docs/content-notes/ and this stops them coming back.
# Scoped to the directory ON PURPOSE: an extension pattern here would silently
# swallow real image assets a future case study needs, and the site would 404
# on them with nothing in git status to show why.
public/images/**/content/

# Impeccable's local state. Three kinds of thing live here and only one of them has any
# lasting value:
#
#   hook.cache.json      the design detector's cache
#   live/server.json     runtime state for the overlay server
#   critique/*.md        the persisted critique snapshots and their score trend
#
# ⚠ THE SNAPSHOTS ARE THE COST OF THIS LINE, AND IT IS WORTH SAYING RATHER THAN DISCOVERING.
# `/impeccable polish` reads them to inherit a run's priority issues, and `critique` reads them
# for the trend it prints. Ignoring the directory makes both LOCAL — a clone, a fresh machine or
# a CI checkout starts with no history, and the 21 -> 22 -> 26 series lives only in this working
# copy. That is the intended trade: the snapshots are a working artifact of a review, not a
# record of the site, and this repository already keeps its durable findings in CLAUDE.md and
# docs/. Anything from a critique worth surviving belongs there instead.
.impeccable/

# ⚠ AND THE TWO FILES THAT SKILL WRITES AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT, FOR THE SAME REASON AND ONE MORE.
# `PRODUCT.md` and `DESIGN.md` are the same kind of artifact as the directory above — a tool's
# working notes about this project, derived from CLAUDE.md, TASKS.md and the shipped code rather
# than authored here. Keeping them local is the same trade: a clone starts without them and loses
# nothing, because everything durable already lives in CLAUDE.md and docs/.
#
# ⚠ `PRODUCT.md` WAS TRACKED FOR ONE COMMIT AND IS UNTRACKED HERE. It reached main inside #603, a
# commit whose subject is about parity panels, because `git add -A` stages whatever is in the tree.
# The file was harmless and the defect was that A COMMIT CARRIED SOMETHING ITS MESSAGE DID NOT
# DESCRIBE. Removing it is the smaller half of that correction; `ralph/tests/no-dev-injection.mjs`
# is the larger half, because the same command nearly shipped a localhost script tag into the root
# layout on the same afternoon.
#
# A DERIVED DOCUMENT IN A REPOSITORY IS A SECOND SOURCE OF TRUTH THAT NOBODY UPDATES. That is the
# durable reason to keep it out, independent of how it got in — this record already carries a dozen
# entries about a claim that ages into being false while still reading as verification.
PRODUCT.md
DESIGN.md
